## Challenges
- Challenges for integration at the cell level: high noise and massive data
  - Matching cell types: very easy
  - Matching cell sub-types: easy
  - Matching individual cells: very difficult because noise overpowers the signal
      - SOTA methods achieve ~ 20% correctness
- My current research aims to match individual cells using a pseudo-likelihood and Gibbs-sampler type approach
  - Drawback: computation time is very long
  - Linear assignment algorithms should achieve the same goal but may be faster

