## Simulation Setup
- Matrix $A$: a 100 x 25 matrix, cell values drawn from $N(0,1)$
- Matrix $B$: $A$ + noise, noise drawn from $N(0,2)$
- Matrix $\tilde{B}$: $B$ with row orders shuffled
- Cost matrix: $C = cor(A, \tilde{B})$
  - $c_{ij}$ is large when $A[i,]$ and $\tilde{B}[j,]$ are similar, i.e. $\tilde{B}[j,] = B[i,]$
- Evaluate the correctness and computation times of the three algorithms under different:
  - Noise levels (the standard deviation of the noise added to $B$)
  - Number of observations
  - Number of features
- 1,000 iterations per scenario
- For the auction algorithm, set $\epsilon = 1/n$ so that we can skip tuning it

